#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
RiftSense v1 Beta — Game History Redesign

Features
--------
DRAFT
- Connects to the local League Client (LCU) while Champion Select is open.
- Detects your assigned role, visible ally picks, visible enemy picks and bans.
- Shows Top 3 composition-fit suggestions from draft_profiles.json.
- Displays champion icons from Riot Data Dragon.
- Never auto-picks/bans or injects; optional rune import writes only a managed rune page.

LIVE GAME
- Reads Riot's local Live Client Data API.
- Displays current item icons.
- Displays a recommended item path and boots using the editable profiles.json file.

Security / transparency
-----------------------
- Source-only Python application.
- No PowerShell.
- No process-memory reading.
- No DLL injection.
- No Riot username/password.
- LCU credentials are read only from League's local lockfile while the client is running.
- LCU reads Champion Select locally; optional rune import writes only /lol-perks/ rune-page endpoints on localhost.
- Live game requests are read-only GET requests to https://127.0.0.1:2999/.
- Internet access is used for Riot Data Dragon assets and optional public meta-source pages used by Meta Consensus.

Important
---------
The League Client API is an unsupported local Riot service and may change after a
League Client update. Draft scores are composition heuristics, not live patch
win-rate statistics.
"""

